WEBVTT

00:07:58.207 --> 00:08:00.727
It was very funny, because
when "Big Magic" came out,

00:08:00.751 --> 00:08:03.532
I was on NPR with this lovely reporter

00:08:03.556 --> 00:08:05.734
who was trying very hard
to take me seriously,

00:08:05.758 --> 00:08:08.908
and said, "You know there are times
when you're reading 'Big Magic'

00:08:08.932 --> 00:08:13.620
where it almost feels as though
you actually believe in magic."

00:08:13.644 --> 00:08:17.470
And she was giving me a doorway
to excuse myself through,

00:08:17.494 --> 00:08:20.958
and I was like, "Oh, no -- I actually
really do totally believe in that."

00:08:20.982 --> 00:08:24.858
You know, thank you for trying to make me
sound serious on National Public Radio,

00:08:24.882 --> 00:08:28.645
but I happen to prefer to live
in an enchanted world,

00:08:28.669 --> 00:08:30.992
but I don't require
that anybody else does.